; recording.chiral -- E197: what a run is asked to record, as a value.
;
; One closed sum names what a run writes down, one constructor per class of
; recordable signal, and one total function prices a request against the run it
; is aimed at. Three classes from the SNN simulator literature: spikes are
; discrete events addressed by occurrence, membrane potential is a continuous
; value existing at every step, synaptic weights are one value per synapse
; moving on a learning timescale.
;
; ⚑ THE INTERVAL'S ABSENCE IS THE STRUCTURAL CLAIM. `record-spikes` carries no
; `sample-every` because an event stream is addressed by occurrence and not by
; time. That is the whole difference between three constructors and one record
; with an optional field, and it moves no volume figure anywhere: `rr-interval`
; is what carries it and tools/test/recording.sh row R5 is what convicts it.
;
; ⚑ INTEGER THROUGHOUT, on decisions/decision-display-numerics. `rate-milli` is
; spikes per neuron per 1,000 ticks, so it reads as Hz when a tick is a
; millisecond, held as an integer because the float wall leaves no other option.
;
; ⚑ `population` IS A `Str` AND THAT IS A DEBT. The boundary-sums directive
; holds that a `Str` encoding which-of-N is a sum in disguise. No `Population`
; type exists: that is arcs/unit-lane-arc row N17 at L4, unminted, and an L2 row
; blocking on an L4 one inverts the lane. The in-tree precedent is `Expert`'s
; `sees` and `returns` at prog/prapanca/core/types.chiral:63, whose own closing row
; N13 is also unminted. Shipping `Str` here mints a second instance of that
; debt, recorded rather than absorbed.
;
; ⚑ THE SCOPE STOPS AT THE REQUEST. The trace itself is arcs/unit-lane-arc row
; N11, unminted, and this file writes into neither `RunManifest` nor `RawCall`:
; the manifest's fifteen fields are the golden manifest's fifteen top-level keys
; and `RawCall`'s comment names the round-trip schema that protects. Any
; population, any projection, any producer of a spike and any storage backend
; are rows N11 through N23 and every one of them is unminted.

(import "prelude/prelude")

; ---- the request ------------------------------------------------------------
;
; ⚑ `sample-every` IS CLOSED AT THE CONSTRUCTOR. `(refine I64 (> 0))` is what
; removes a zero divide and a negative volume before a binary exists: `0` and
; `-3` are refused with `load: cannot prove refinement`. The engine decides the
; predicate for a literal and for a value already at the refined type, and
; refuses every computed argument including `(+ 20 5)`, so every caller between
; the literal and this constructor carries the refined type in its OWN
; signature. An ordinary `I64` seat fails the whole root with no site named.
; `>` and `<` are two of the five legal refinement operators (`SymOp`,
; lib/typing/refine.chiral:11).
(data RecordRequest ()
  (record-spikes   (population Str))
  (record-membrane (population Str) (sample-every (refine I64 (> 0))))
  (record-weights  (population Str) (sample-every (refine I64 (> 0)))))

; ---- the run a request is priced against ------------------------------------

(data RunShape ()
  (run-shape (neurons I64) (fanout I64) (ticks I64) (rate-milli I64)))

; ---- what a pricing answers -------------------------------------------------
;
; ⚑ COMMISSIONING NOTHING IS A REASON, NOT A ZERO. With the refinement in place
; a zero divide and a negative volume are gone at compile time, so the second
; arm holds one case: the interval outran the run. On an `I64` return that case
; prints 0, and 0 is a legitimate volume elsewhere in the type, since a request
; over a population at `rate-milli = 0` prices honestly at zero. One integer
; would then carry two unrelated facts. That is the collision
; definitions/pattern-boundary-sums names and E196's `DecodeR` already answers
; one layer up.
;
; ⚑ THERE IS NO `v-unbounded` AND THE WRAP IS UNGUARDED. Reporting the `I64`
; wrap before the multiply needs either a high-half product, which is
; arcs/unit-lane-arc row N1 and unminted, or a division pre-check on every
; factor, which `RunShape`'s unrefined fields do not support. The wall sits at
; 10^18 samples, an exabyte at one byte per sample, so the sweep pins the wrap
; as observed behaviour and this type guards nothing.
(data VolumeR ()
  (v-ok (samples I64))
  (v-empty))

; a product of zero is a request that commissions nothing.
(def rr-wrap (-> I64 VolumeR)
  (lam (v) (case (=i v 0) (true (v-empty)) (false (v-ok v)))))

; ---- the pricing ------------------------------------------------------------
;
; ONE total function over the sum. Three arms, no `_`, integer only, and `->`
; because a request is inert data and pricing it crosses nothing.
;
;   spikes    every neuron's events over the whole run, at the firing rate
;   membrane  one value per neuron per sampled step
;   weights   one value per synapse per sampled step
;
; The division is the tree's `/`, which floors, so an interval exceeding the run
; gives a quotient of zero and `rr-wrap` folds the product to `v-empty`.
(declare rr-samples (-> RunShape RecordRequest VolumeR))
(def rr-samples (lam (s q)
  (case s
    ((run-shape n f t r)
      (case q
        ((record-spikes p)     (rr-wrap (/ (* (* n t) r) 1000)))
        ((record-membrane p e) (rr-wrap (* n (/ t e))))
        ((record-weights p e)  (rr-wrap (* (* n f) (/ t e)))))))))

; ---- the interval, typed ----------------------------------------------------
;
; The `none` arm IS the asymmetry: it is what a conventional `sampling_interval=`
; keyword cannot say.
(declare rr-interval (-> RecordRequest (Maybe I64)))
(def rr-interval (lam (q)
  (case q
    ((record-spikes p)     none)
    ((record-membrane p e) (some e))
    ((record-weights p e)  (some e)))))

; ---- the digest -------------------------------------------------------------
;
; What a manifest would keep: bounded, and constant in the run's length. The
; sweep's `fields=` column beside its `samples=` column is the contrast the
; element exists to express, and it is why the request cannot be folded into the
; trace it commissions.
;
; ⚑ WHAT THE DIGEST BECOMES IS NOT ANSWERED HERE. Whether it is a field on row
; N11's trace type, a separate small record, or this function and nothing more
; is N11's answer to give, and N11 is unminted.
(declare rr-fields (-> RecordRequest I64))
(def rr-fields (lam (q)
  (case q
    ((record-spikes p)     1)
    ((record-membrane p e) 2)
    ((record-weights p e)  2))))
